1
00:00:13,291 --> 00:00:16,458
Don't leave me alone

2
00:00:16,958 --> 00:00:19,125
Don't leave me alone

3
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:24,166
Trembling in the dark night

4
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:28,583
Don't leave me alone Don't leave me…

5
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:31,625
SHENG 2026 CONCERT
"DON'T LEAVE ME ALONE" HITS GLOBAL SUCCESS

6
00:00:31,708 --> 00:00:34,208
I'm used to having you around

7
00:00:34,291 --> 00:00:37,791
I really can't lose you

8
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:42,666
If you still love me

9
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:48,333
Can you hold me tight again?

10
00:00:51,458 --> 00:00:52,625
Thank you.

11
00:00:53,791 --> 00:00:55,166
You're like my family.

12
00:00:56,958 --> 00:00:58,166
Without you,

13
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,458
I wouldn't be here.

14
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,875
THE FIXERS

15
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:29,541
NIGHT AND DAY

16
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:33,041
Attorney Chao Ming-cheng
dropped a bombshell earlier today

17
00:01:33,125 --> 00:01:34,833
at the Ming Young Party's fundraiser,

18
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:37,375
releasing a video clip of his son
being framed by mobsters.

19
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:03,458
I'm happy you're here.

20
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:05,083
Dad hates it when I come.

21
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,916
Otherwise, I'd go to
all these shallow social events.

22
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:12,666
-Make sure he stays out of trouble.
-Um, sure.

23
00:02:18,916 --> 00:02:21,083
Fortune, I told you
you can't play with that one.

24
00:02:21,166 --> 00:02:22,666
Find another one. Go.

25
00:03:02,375 --> 00:03:04,583
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

26
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:07,333
-You've been training.
-Just talent with the ball.

27
00:03:10,541 --> 00:03:14,708
Two years' practice can't match
your brother's three months of training.

28
00:03:15,458 --> 00:03:17,208
Use two hands on your backhand.

29
00:03:17,291 --> 00:03:19,000
You could have won earlier.

30
00:03:19,541 --> 00:03:23,208
Dragging out a win will still count
as a loss. Hear what I'm saying?

31
00:03:25,166 --> 00:03:26,291
You did a good job.

32
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:28,541
Very good.

33
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:31,208
Keep it up.

34
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:35,666
Hmm.

35
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,250
-Sir.
-Ah, hello.

36
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:41,833
Tristan, come with me.
Come say hi to the speaker.

37
00:03:43,291 --> 00:03:44,583
-Hello, sir.
-Hello there.

38
00:03:44,666 --> 00:03:46,416
-This is Tristan.
-Ah.

39
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,375
You should have said that you were here.

40
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:50,208
You were all so busy.

41
00:03:50,791 --> 00:03:52,333
What would we be busy with?

42
00:04:02,166 --> 00:04:04,291
Howie, time for breakfast.

43
00:04:04,375 --> 00:04:07,000
Brooding heartthrob Sheng
wooed fans last night…

44
00:04:07,083 --> 00:04:10,041
So, where did you go last night?

45
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:13,125
When you used to finish a big job,
you'd come home, and you'd channel surf.

46
00:04:13,708 --> 00:04:14,833
Tell me if you're in trouble.

47
00:04:15,458 --> 00:04:19,041
What do you mean by trouble?
My biggest trouble's standing over there.

48
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:20,333
You can say that again.

49
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:24,708
Who could that be this early?

50
00:04:28,875 --> 00:04:31,083
Uh, and you are?

51
00:04:31,666 --> 00:04:33,416
Does Felix Chiang live here?

52
00:04:34,166 --> 00:04:35,791
Yeah.

53
00:04:36,458 --> 00:04:37,708
Felix.

54
00:04:38,208 --> 00:04:39,375
-Yeah?
-It's for you.

55
00:04:39,875 --> 00:04:42,125
Sheng's new album has been released…

56
00:04:42,208 --> 00:04:44,416
-I am from Ching He Temple.
-Ching He?

57
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,750
I'd like you to come with me.

58
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:49,541
We'd like to talk to you at Ching He.

59
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:54,458
Uh, I didn't donate a lot last year.

60
00:04:54,541 --> 00:04:56,625
But thank you for the recognition.

61
00:05:02,875 --> 00:05:04,125
Uh, sure.

62
00:05:07,541 --> 00:05:10,250
Howie, finish what you're doing.
Get off to school now.

63
00:05:17,333 --> 00:05:20,083
Oh, big shot now, are you?

64
00:05:20,708 --> 00:05:22,666
You've gone from cop car to luxury car.

65
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:25,958
Milky, I'm busy now.
I'll make tea another day, huh?

66
00:05:26,041 --> 00:05:26,875
You kidding me?

67
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:29,500
Fuck tea. You're dead
unless you pay me what you owe.

68
00:05:31,791 --> 00:05:32,625
Milky.

69
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,916
Can I ask if you'd like to come with us
to Ching He for tea?

70
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,750
The boss is talking. Don't cut in.

71
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:38,708
Quiet!

72
00:05:39,208 --> 00:05:40,416
Sir, I'm sorry.

73
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:43,083
The young ones, you know?
Let me open the door for you.

74
00:05:44,333 --> 00:05:45,375
Sir.

75
00:05:46,833 --> 00:05:48,041
Don't grovel, all right?

76
00:05:48,125 --> 00:05:49,250
There's a good boy.

77
00:05:57,708 --> 00:05:58,833
Who are those people?

78
00:05:59,416 --> 00:06:03,500
The boss once told me
that if I ever run into Ching He's people,

79
00:06:03,583 --> 00:06:05,208
then to stay far away.

80
00:06:05,291 --> 00:06:07,833
Our friend's gonna wind up
swamp eel noodles.

81
00:06:07,916 --> 00:06:08,958
Damn it.

82
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Sir.

83
00:06:18,375 --> 00:06:19,208
Hey.

84
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,625
The chairman of Ching He, Thackery Huang.

85
00:06:22,708 --> 00:06:24,291
Thank you for your help.

86
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:27,583
Oh, don't worry.
I promise I'll keep last night a secret.

87
00:06:27,666 --> 00:06:29,291
-Ah.
-My mouth's like my liver.

88
00:06:29,375 --> 00:06:30,458
They're both made of steel.

89
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:34,750
-Do you remember Sir Hong?
-I don't recall where I slept last night.

90
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:35,875
Do you recall San He?

91
00:06:36,791 --> 00:06:39,041
You protected someone for them,
and they were killed.

92
00:06:39,125 --> 00:06:40,458
Do you recall that? Do you?

93
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:41,375
Uh…

94
00:06:41,458 --> 00:06:44,500
Ten years ago, Black Bull,
the leader of Chamber Thirteen.

95
00:06:44,583 --> 00:06:45,958
You know who took him out?

96
00:06:46,041 --> 00:06:47,125
It was me.

97
00:06:49,958 --> 00:06:53,000
Sir, I don't doubt what you're saying.

98
00:06:53,083 --> 00:06:55,625
But I don't know this person Black Bull.

99
00:06:55,708 --> 00:06:57,208
I think you must be mistaken.

100
00:06:58,458 --> 00:07:02,250
When you and Chen Liang-chi
were fighting for control of San He…

101
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,625
…nobody could rival you,

102
00:07:05,708 --> 00:07:07,000
you in particular.

103
00:07:07,083 --> 00:07:08,791
You never killed.

104
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:13,833
You'd only destroy their kneecaps.

105
00:07:16,666 --> 00:07:17,750
Sir,

106
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:20,000
I was just trying to make a living.

107
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:22,958
Hmm. It's been over a decade.

108
00:07:23,458 --> 00:07:25,625
Your aim is still as sharp as ever.

109
00:07:26,125 --> 00:07:27,125
Would you consider

110
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:30,000
doing work for us here?

111
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:33,000
It's not possible.
I'm not as sharp as I once was.

112
00:07:33,083 --> 00:07:34,583
And this hand…

113
00:07:34,666 --> 00:07:37,708
Uh, long story short,
I can't really work for you.

114
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,833
From what I hear,

115
00:07:39,916 --> 00:07:41,833
you're in need of some help lately.

116
00:07:41,916 --> 00:07:44,291
If you decide to work for us,

117
00:07:44,958 --> 00:07:46,500
you'll have enough money.

118
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:57,291
Well, that's not really necessary.

119
00:07:57,791 --> 00:08:00,833
I just want my family safe
and you not to visit the house.

120
00:08:00,916 --> 00:08:04,500
May our paths never cross again,
and may we each enjoy our own freedoms.

121
00:08:05,125 --> 00:08:06,791
See you, bye. Bye.

122
00:08:13,291 --> 00:08:17,333
I… wonder
if there are other candidates around.

123
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:19,541
Give him some time.

124
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:21,958
He'll return to Ching He.

125
00:08:34,708 --> 00:08:36,375
Fortune.

126
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:40,833
Wait. Go.

127
00:08:42,666 --> 00:08:45,333
That's all.
Remember what the vet said to you.

128
00:08:46,416 --> 00:08:47,541
Peace.

129
00:08:47,625 --> 00:08:48,750
This is it.

130
00:08:59,125 --> 00:09:02,125
The super popular idol Sheng
has done it again.

131
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:05,125
He's breaking all sales records
with the release of his new album.

132
00:09:05,208 --> 00:09:07,041
SHENG ANNOUNCES TAIPEI ARENA CONCERT

133
00:09:19,583 --> 00:09:21,583
All right. Sit.

134
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,250
Good dog. Wait here.

135
00:09:24,333 --> 00:09:25,291
See you tonight.

136
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:33,166
Welcome.
The bread's just fresh out of the oven.

137
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,375
Give me a three-in-one combo, sir.

138
00:09:36,458 --> 00:09:38,000
One three-in-one.

139
00:09:38,083 --> 00:09:40,125
Pineapple, scallion, pork floss.

140
00:09:40,208 --> 00:09:41,958
-Make it hot.
-Okay.

141
00:09:42,041 --> 00:09:43,750
Hey. Feeling better?

142
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,416
Yeah, I'm all fine now.

143
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,375
It was nothing.
I've survived worse than that.

144
00:09:47,458 --> 00:09:49,416
Oh, tough guy, are you?

145
00:09:50,791 --> 00:09:53,000
Three-in-one combo, ready to go.

146
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,250
Your wife ask any questions?

147
00:09:56,125 --> 00:09:59,166
I saw a babe, got distracted and crashed.

148
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:00,875
She believed that, did she?

149
00:10:00,958 --> 00:10:02,208
Mm.

150
00:10:02,916 --> 00:10:03,791
Thank you.

151
00:10:05,583 --> 00:10:06,416
Here.

152
00:10:09,416 --> 00:10:13,250
Mm. You come straight home after. Okay?

153
00:10:21,291 --> 00:10:22,666
What are you laughing at?

154
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,000
We need dressing. We're out.

155
00:10:27,083 --> 00:10:29,000
Okay.

156
00:10:32,875 --> 00:10:33,875
-Here.
-What's this?

157
00:10:33,958 --> 00:10:35,166
It's for your son.

158
00:10:35,666 --> 00:10:37,791
He could have gotten it from you just now.

159
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:42,583
It means more if it's from his dad.

160
00:10:45,708 --> 00:10:48,500
Hey. Has the chairman said
who's replacing me?

161
00:10:48,583 --> 00:10:51,875
I'm sure he'll agree
that I should work on my own.

162
00:10:53,375 --> 00:10:55,916
You should know he'd never do that.

163
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,500
He'd never agree to anything
that violates the rules.

164
00:10:58,583 --> 00:11:01,125
CHING HE TEMPLE: EIGHT O'CLOCK TONIGHT

165
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:04,541
Chen Chia-yun.

166
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:06,875
Food's here.

167
00:11:13,791 --> 00:11:14,958
Chen Chia-yun?

168
00:11:32,708 --> 00:11:34,625
Aren't you sick of watching this?

169
00:11:35,125 --> 00:11:36,375
Don't scare me like that.

170
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:38,541
What happened to you?

171
00:11:38,625 --> 00:11:39,916
Who hurt you?

172
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,125
-Rabid dog.
-A dog? Really?

173
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,375
I got you a 70/30.

174
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,583
Oh! My ticket!

175
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:51,250
Aw! Sheng's face is dirty now,

176
00:11:51,333 --> 00:11:52,833
and it's all wet.

177
00:11:52,916 --> 00:11:54,166
Why'd you do that?

178
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:55,166
Hey.

179
00:11:58,041 --> 00:11:58,875
Oh.

180
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:01,583
This ticket, it's making you stressed.

181
00:12:01,666 --> 00:12:04,000
It's a concert I've been waiting ages for,
all right?

182
00:12:04,083 --> 00:12:06,000
-You're going with a guy?
-Why say that?

183
00:12:06,083 --> 00:12:07,708
You're going with a boyfriend, aren't you?

184
00:12:07,791 --> 00:12:10,208
-I'm not.
-"I'm not. I'm not."

185
00:12:10,291 --> 00:12:13,083
Hey, this was in the mail.
Looks important, huh?

186
00:12:17,041 --> 00:12:18,708
What is it?

187
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,250
The US exam board
sent an acceptance letter!

188
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:23,333
Oh yeah!

189
00:12:23,416 --> 00:12:25,958
The temple towers loom tall.
Like father, like daughter.

190
00:12:26,708 --> 00:12:28,583
-You're in luck.
-I just thought I'd try it

191
00:12:28,666 --> 00:12:30,166
I don't have to do it.

192
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:33,375
Don't worry about money. That's my part.

193
00:12:33,458 --> 00:12:36,125
I can make it after I graduate.

194
00:12:36,208 --> 00:12:38,708
Your father and I never achieved much,

195
00:12:38,791 --> 00:12:40,416
but luckily you got your mom's brains.

196
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,708
You get a chance, you go for it.

197
00:12:42,791 --> 00:12:44,750
I'll sort out money.

198
00:12:47,666 --> 00:12:48,500
Hello?

199
00:12:49,041 --> 00:12:51,125
Hello there.
I'm calling from Hsing Tai Bank.

200
00:12:51,208 --> 00:12:53,083
-Are you Mr. Chiang?
-Yes, I am.

201
00:12:53,166 --> 00:12:54,833
This is a courtesy call to remind you

202
00:12:54,916 --> 00:12:57,416
that your loan payment for the month
hasn't been paid.

203
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,583
-Eat something.
-It's already overdue.

204
00:12:59,666 --> 00:13:01,291
Please handle it as soon as possible

205
00:13:01,375 --> 00:13:03,500
to avoid
your credit rating being affected.

206
00:13:03,583 --> 00:13:04,458
Okay.

207
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:07,166
Okay, I understand.

208
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:08,625
Thank you. Thank you.

209
00:13:23,708 --> 00:13:25,333
Parkinson's disease?

210
00:13:28,083 --> 00:13:29,791
That makes no sense.

211
00:13:30,291 --> 00:13:32,958
I don't know if I've had
a serious illness ever.

212
00:13:33,041 --> 00:13:35,375
I've only hurt my right hand.

213
00:13:35,458 --> 00:13:37,958
Your situation is relatively uncommon.

214
00:13:38,041 --> 00:13:39,791
You have concurrent action tremors

215
00:13:39,875 --> 00:13:41,541
apart from what you're getting
in your hand.

216
00:13:43,125 --> 00:13:45,291
Uh, how is this treated?

217
00:13:45,791 --> 00:13:47,791
Will my left hand go the same way?

218
00:13:47,875 --> 00:13:51,958
The disease is caused by the degeneration
of substantia nigra cells in the brain.

219
00:13:52,041 --> 00:13:55,166
-Dopamine secretion will--
-Hey, hey, Doctor, clearer, clearer.

220
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:56,166
It's incurable,

221
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:58,208
if you want to hear it clearer.

222
00:13:58,791 --> 00:14:02,625
However, active treatment
and medication can delay its progression.

223
00:14:06,083 --> 00:14:08,125
So, after that,

224
00:14:09,041 --> 00:14:10,750
then what then?

225
00:14:11,583 --> 00:14:16,041
Some patients experience disability
or dementia in the final stages.

226
00:14:16,541 --> 00:14:18,416
But the rate of progression can vary.

227
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:22,208
Some patients go from the initial stage
to final stage in three months,

228
00:14:22,291 --> 00:14:25,625
but, uh, some patients do better
and might have ten years or more.

229
00:14:29,416 --> 00:14:33,083
Sweetheart,
after Howie finishes his exams,

230
00:14:33,166 --> 00:14:36,958
let's go on an overseas holiday.
I've never taken you guys abroad.

231
00:14:48,041 --> 00:14:51,083
The chairman says that you can go in now.

232
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:52,041
Okay.

233
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:14,083
You should know
I won't do anything unethical.

234
00:15:14,708 --> 00:15:18,833
You don't need to worry.
We're not killers or even criminals.

235
00:15:18,916 --> 00:15:19,833
TAI SUI HALL

236
00:15:19,916 --> 00:15:22,416
We just help people take care of problems.

237
00:15:24,166 --> 00:15:26,958
This type of fish is called a cleaner.

238
00:15:27,875 --> 00:15:30,291
They like to hide in murky water.

239
00:15:30,791 --> 00:15:34,625
They have no natural predators
and are extremely resilient.

240
00:15:35,708 --> 00:15:38,125
But humans don't like them.

241
00:15:38,666 --> 00:15:41,500
They think they're dirty and smelly.

242
00:15:42,458 --> 00:15:47,166
But without them, the water would be
too polluted for anything to survive in.

243
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:51,375
Ching He's fixers
are just like this type of fish.

244
00:15:51,458 --> 00:15:53,791
Business identities, politicians,

245
00:15:53,875 --> 00:15:55,541
whichever side of the law,

246
00:15:56,041 --> 00:16:00,000
when they have a situation
they can't handle personally,

247
00:16:00,083 --> 00:16:05,125
they'll hire us
to discreetly clean up the mess for them.

248
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:10,875
We try to stay above
both sides of the law.

249
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:13,375
We never play favorites.

250
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:15,750
Here, you won't go by your name.

251
00:16:15,833 --> 00:16:17,708
You'll have a code name.

252
00:16:17,791 --> 00:16:19,458
Oh? Well, that's easy.

253
00:16:19,541 --> 00:16:22,333
See, people call me Swamp Eel.

254
00:16:28,833 --> 00:16:31,083
CHING HE

255
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:38,875
We choose all code names for fixers
from the Thousand Character Classic.

256
00:16:38,958 --> 00:16:39,875
So what's mine?

257
00:16:43,541 --> 00:16:44,500
What's this about?

258
00:16:45,166 --> 00:16:46,416
What? You again?

259
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,791
Let me tell you, you're still on my radar.

260
00:16:48,875 --> 00:16:52,583
This is Fixer Gold.
And from now on, he's your partner.

261
00:16:53,291 --> 00:16:54,166
